{{also|hof|Hoff|hóf}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|hof}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*hufą||hill, farm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hoːf/|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/hɔf/|lang=de}} {{a|northern and western Germany; becoming rare}}
* {{audio|De-at-Hof.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Hof.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Hofes|gen2=Hofs|Höfe|Höfchen}}

# [[yard]], [[court]], [[courtyard]] {{gloss|open area by a house or enclosed by houses}}
#: ''Der '''Hof''' hinter unserm Haus ist mit Schiefer gepflastert.''
#:: The '''yard''' behind our house is paved with slate.
# [[court]] {{gloss|residence and entourage of a nobleman}}
#: ''Am '''Hof''' des Königs gab es ständige Intrigen.''
#:: There were constant intrigues at the king's '''court'''.
# [[farmyard]] {{gloss|central area of a farm, excluding the fields}}
#: ''Das Essen wird den Arbeitern ins Feld gebracht, damit sie erst abends auf den '''Hof''' zurückkommen müssen.''
#:: The workers are served food in the fields, so that they needn’t come back to the '''farmyard''' before the evening.
# {{lb|de|by extension}} [[farm]], [[agricultural]] [[enterprise]]
#: ''Wenn mein Sohn den '''Hof''' nicht übernimmt, muss ich verkaufen.''
#:: If my son doesn’t take over the '''farm''', I’ll have to sell it.

